# Fairness + reaction-budget overlay for the ArduPilot-OA arm of the
# comparison. Loaded AFTER config/oa.parm, which it deliberately does not
# modify -- that file is the shared BendyRuler setup, this one holds only the
# choices that exist because we are comparing against Nav2.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The first OA run flew into block_west at (-30, 25) and crashed. The proximity
# chain was fine (verified: /lidar/scan 403 finite returns at 5 Hz, ArduPilot
# emitting DISTANCE_SENSOR and 80 OA-database objects). The vehicle was simply
# going too fast to use any of it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Speed: match the Nav2 arm
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ArduCopter 4.8 renamed WPNAV_SPEED -> WP_SPD, and the units changed from cm/s
# to m/s (AC_WPNav.cpp: _wp_speed_ms). The default is 10 m/s. Nav2's MPPI is
# capped at vx_max/vy_max = 1.0 m/s, so the stock ArduPilot vehicle was flying
# the same course TEN TIMES faster -- not a comparison, just a different
# experiment. At 10 m/s the reaction budget was about a second:
#   OA_DB_DIST_MAX 10 m  -> 1.0 s of warning
#   OA_BR_LOOKAHEAD 8 m  -> 0.8 s
#   PRX_FILT 0.25 Hz     -> ~0.6 s of lag on the distances themselves
# i.e. the filtered obstacle appeared at roughly the moment of impact.
WP_SPD           1.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Proximity filter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# oa.parm sets 0.25 Hz and its own comment says "raise toward 1.0 if BendyRuler
# reacts too late". The scan arrives at 5 Hz, so 0.25 Hz throws away almost all
# of it. 2.0 Hz still smooths the per-ray noise (stddev 0.02 m in the model)
# without hiding an approaching wall.
PRX_FILT         2.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT changed, so the two stacks stay comparable
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   OA_DB_DIST_MAX 10  ~ Nav2 obstacle_max_range 8.0  (similar sensing horizon)
#   OA_MARGIN_MAX   5  ~ Nav2 inflation_radius  4.0   (similar standoff)
# Changing either would hand one stack an advantage the other does not have.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ONE THAT MAKES OA ACTUALLY RUN
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GUID_OPTIONS bit 6 (64) = "Waypoint navigation used for position targets".
#
# Without it, a GUIDED position target from SET_POSITION_TARGET_LOCAL_NED goes
# to ModeGuided::pos_control_start() -> SubMode::Pos, which drives pos_control
# directly. AP_OAPathPlanner lives inside AC_WPNav::update_wpnav(), so that
# path NEVER CONSULTS THE OBJECT AVOIDANCE PLANNER. BendyRuler is configured,
# the proximity sensor works, the OA database fills with objects -- and the
# vehicle flies straight through them, because nothing on that code path asks
# the planner anything.
#
# With bit 6 set, ModeGuided::set_destination() takes the
# use_wpnav_for_position_control() branch instead: SubMode::WP via
# wp_nav->set_wp_destination_NED_m(), which does run OA.
#   ArduCopter/mode_guided.cpp:380 and :670
#   ArduCopter/mode.h:1213          WPNavUsedForPosControl = (1U << 6)
#   ArduCopter/Parameters.cpp:825   GUID_OPTIONS default 0
#
# Diagnosed the hard way: two crashes into block_west at (-30, 25), first at
# the 10 m/s default and again after WP_SPD was matched to Nav2's 1 m/s. The
# speed fix above was necessary but not sufficient -- OA was never consulted
# at either speed.
GUID_OPTIONS     64
